sshd is running on port 22 with password authentication enabled. Next up is nginx: self-signed certificate + server block on 8443.

Certificate:
```
mkdir -p /etc/nginx/ssl
openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout /etc/nginx/ssl/localhost.key -out /etc/nginx/ssl/localhost.crt -subj "/CN=localhost" -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:localhost,IP:127.0.0.1"
```

Config — use a single root /var/www/git-deploy, and handle /dev via a subdirectory (the hook will check out dev to /var/www/git-deploy/dev).

/etc/nginx/sites-available/git-deploy:
```
server {
    listen 8443 ssl;
    listen [::]:8443 ssl;
    server_name localhost;
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/localhost.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/localhost.key;
    root /var/www/git-deploy;
    index index.html;
    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }
}
```

Then symlink it into sites-enabled, test the config, and start nginx.

After that, the post-receive hook.

